/*
 * The circle-cube emblem, as an alternative to the hierophant. THREE FRAMES.
 *
 * Generated from ~/src/models123/circle_cube_simple.py, NOT from the original
 * artwork. That script exists because the full design carries features 0.4% of
 * its diameter -- fine at 140mm, invisible at 13mm -- and redraws it so nothing
 * is narrower than FINEST_FEATURE. A 144px 1-bit panel is the same constraint
 * as a small engraving, and the same answer serves both.
 *
 * FINEST_FEATURE is 2.36mm against a 138.6mm design diameter, so at 144 pixels
 * wide the narrowest surviving feature is 2.5px. The full-detail emblem was
 * tried first and is unusable here: its hatching and beading fall below one
 * pixel, and thresholding turns the whole disc into noise.
 *
 * THE ANIMATION. In the script the cube is a frame only -- its three faces are
 * cut out of the silhouette and left as clean voids. Each frame below shades
 * exactly one of them, so cycling the frames turns the cube. Nothing outside
 * the cube differs between frames.
 *
 * The shading is a 50% CHECKERBOARD -- alternate pixels, (x + y) even. It is
 * applied to the finished bitmap, not to the model: a one-pixel checker in
 * build123d would be far under FINEST_FEATURE and rasterising it would either
 * erase it or turn it to noise. Straight onto the bitmap it is exact, one
 * checker pixel per panel pixel, with no resampling in between. A face costs
 * about 460 pixels, so the emblem goes from 36% ink bare to 38% shaded.
 *
 * FRAME ORDER IS CLOCKWISE ON SCREEN: top, lower-right, lower-left. That is
 * NOT the model's FACE_ANGLES order (90, 210, 330), which runs the other way;
 * the generator reorders them deliberately. Swap the two lower faces to turn
 * the cube back the other way.
 *
 * 144x144, 1bpp MSB first, 18 bytes per row. A circle rather than the
 * hierophant's spear, so all four corners are free.
 *
 * To regenerate, with the model venv (PYTHONPATH must be cleared or the nix
 * PIL shadows the venv's):
 *     env -u PYTHONPATH ~/src/models123/.venv/bin/python circlecube_gen.py
 * The generator is kept beside this file. Do not hand-edit the arrays. It
 * reproduces the bare emblem at exactly 7401 ink pixels, which is what the
 * pre-animation version of this file carried -- a useful check that the
 * pipeline still lands where it used to.
 *
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
 */

